# =============================================================================
# Rawura — Main-server (Express + Mongoose REST API)
#
# The core commerce API: products, orders, carts, payments, shipping, settings,
# and all transactional email. Serves the storefront (:3009) and admin (:4999).
#
# Runs on:  http://localhost:3000   (PORT below; code default is 4000 if unset)
#
# Usage:
#     cp .env.example .env
#     # fill in the placeholders, then:
#     npm install && npm run dev
#
# Loading: dotenv is called at the top of src/server.ts; nodemon also preloads
# `-r dotenv/config`. Every script in scripts/ calls dotenv.config() itself and
# reads this same file.
#
# Boot order / dependencies:
#   1. MongoDB must be reachable (Atlas or local) — the server exits if not.
#   2. RabbitMQ should be up before this service, or event publishing silently
#      degrades. Start rabbit (or CloudAMQP) first.
#   3. event-bus and websocket-gateway consume events this service publishes;
#      start them AFTER this one. This service does not call them directly.
#   4. Storefront/admin revalidation URLs are called on settings save only —
#      those services can be down at boot without breaking anything here.
#
# This service OWNS the store brand (src/services/brand): it resolves every
# value in the "Email — brand" section from the Settings document, then these
# env vars, then hardcoded fallbacks, and serves the result to event-bus and the
# storefront. The `@rawura/emails` package never reads brand values. It reads
# only its transport config from process.env: the "Email — SMTP" section,
# FROM_EMAIL, EMAIL_TEMPLATE_NO_CACHE and CDN_BASE_URL.
#
# NEVER commit a filled-in .env.
#
# Two kinds of value appear below:
#   - `<angle-bracket text>` and `xxxx…` are PLACEHOLDERS. You must replace them.
#   - Everything else (PORT, CORS_ORIGINS, NODE_ENV, the localhost URLs, the
#     numeric timeouts, STORE_* brand defaults) is a working local-dev value you
#     can leave as-is.
#
# WARNING: a placeholder is still a non-empty string, so `cp .env.example .env`
# and `npm run dev` WILL boot — the `if (!JWT_SECRET) throw` guards in
# src/middleware/auth.ts see the literal placeholder text and pass. The server
# coming up is NOT evidence that you filled these in. Replace every placeholder.
# =============================================================================


# ---- Core ----

# Node environment. Not read by src/ directly — set by the `qa` and `prod` npm
# scripts. Safe to set here for local parity.
# OPTIONAL — no code reads it; libraries (express) default to development.
NODE_ENV=development

# HTTP port the API listens on.
# OPTIONAL — code falls back to 4000, but every other service in the monorepo
# is configured to call :3000. Set it.
PORT=3000

# Comma-separated list of allowed CORS origins (trimmed per entry).
# OPTIONAL — falls back to ['http://localhost:3009','http://localhost:4999'].
# In production this MUST list every storefront/admin domain or the browser
# blocks all API calls.
CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3009,http://localhost:4999


# ---- Database ----

# MongoDB connection string. Atlas SRV or a local mongod.
# REQUIRED — src/lib/db.ts throws 'MongoDB URI is not defined' and the server
# never starts without it.
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://<user>:<password>@<cluster>.mongodb.net/<database>

# Alias for MONGODB_URI, read only by scripts/ and scripts/migrations/ as a
# second choice (`MONGODB_URI || DATABASE_URL`).
# OPTIONAL — leave unset if MONGODB_URI is set; nothing in src/ reads it.
# DATABASE_URL=mongodb+srv://<user>:<password>@<cluster>.mongodb.net/<database>

# Legacy alias read by exactly one script (scripts/migrate-packSizes.ts), which
# falls back to mongodb://localhost:27017/oeplast — i.e. it will happily connect
# to the WRONG database if this is unset. Set it before running that migration.
# OPTIONAL — only needed for `migrate-packSizes`.
# MONGO_URI=mongodb+srv://<user>:<password>@<cluster>.mongodb.net/<database>

# Name of the MongoDB Atlas Search index used by product search
# (src/services/productService.ts).
# OPTIONAL — falls back to 'default'. Only change if your Atlas index is named
# something else; a wrong name makes search fall back / return nothing.
ATLAS_SEARCH_INDEX=default


# ---- Auth & secrets ----

# Signs and verifies all JWTs (src/lib/tokenizer.ts, src/middleware/auth.ts).
# REQUIRED — auth.ts and tokenizer.ts throw 'Set JWT secret' at import time; the
# server will not boot.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
JWT_SECRET=<64-char-hex — generate with: openssl rand -hex 32>

# Google OAuth client ID(s) that sign-in ID tokens are checked against
# (src/lib/googleIdToken.ts). Same value as the storefront's GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID /
# AUTH_GOOGLE_ID; comma-separate several clients. REQUIRED for Google sign-in —
# when unset, /auth/login/provider refuses every login instead of trusting the
# account id sent in the request.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=<your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com>

# Number of reverse-proxy / load-balancer hops in front of this server (usually 1).
# Rate limits key on the client IP; behind a proxy, leave this unset and every
# customer shares the proxy's IP. OPTIONAL — leave unset when clients connect directly.
# TRUST_PROXY=1

# Shared secret for service-to-service calls on /internal/* routes; callers send
# it as a header. Also the last-resort fallback for UNSUBSCRIBE_SECRET.
# REQUIRED — auth.ts throws 'Set INTERNAL_SERVICE_KEY in environment variables'
# at import time. Must match the same value in event-bus and websocket-gateway.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
INTERNAL_SERVICE_KEY=<64-char-hex — shared with event-bus / websocket-gateway>

# Server-side pepper mixed into every password before bcrypt (src/lib/password.ts).
# REQUIRED — and it fails SILENTLY, which is the dangerous part. password.ts does
# `password + PEPPER` with no guard, so when this is unset every hash is peppered
# with the literal 7-character string "undefined". Nothing throws, nothing logs,
# logins keep working — you just have a publicly-known pepper.
# CHANGING IT INVALIDATES EVERY EXISTING PASSWORD HASH (including the accidental
# "undefined" ones). Set it once per environment, before the first user signs up,
# and never rotate it without a password-reset migration.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
PEPPER_SECRET=<64-char-hex — generate with: openssl rand -hex 32>

# HMAC key for one-click email unsubscribe tokens (src/utils/unsubscribeToken.ts).
# OPTIONAL — falls back to JWT_SECRET, then INTERNAL_SERVICE_KEY, then ''.
# REQUIRED — currently MISSING from .env; unsubscribe links are therefore signed
# with the same key as session tokens, and rotating JWT_SECRET silently breaks
# every unsubscribe link already sitting in customers' inboxes. Set a dedicated one.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
UNSUBSCRIBE_SECRET=<64-char-hex — generate with: openssl rand -hex 32>


# ---- Payments (Paystack) ----

# Paystack secret key. Used for transaction initialize, verify, refund, AND as
# the default webhook-signature secret.
# REQUIRED — checkout, payment verification and refunds all fail without it.
# Get it from: Paystack dashboard → Settings → API Keys & Webhooks.
# Use sk_test_… in development; sk_live_… only in production.
PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Dedicated secret for verifying the x-paystack-signature webhook HMAC.
# OPTIONAL — code does `PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY || PAYSTACK_WEBHOOK_SECRET`, so the
# secret key is used when this is unset. Only set it if Paystack issues you a
# distinct webhook secret.
# PAYSTACK_WEBHOOK_SECRET=<paystack webhook secret>

# URL Paystack redirects the customer back to after payment; passed as
# `callback_url` on transaction initialize (src/services/TransactionService.ts:63).
# OPTIONAL today — the storefront pays via the Paystack INLINE POPUP
# (`@paystack/inline-js`, popup.resumeTransaction in src/hooks/useCheckoutController.ts),
# which never redirects, so the happy path ignores callback_url entirely. It only
# takes effect on Paystack's redirect-based channels and on its hosted fallback
# page. Unset today, so those paths land on whatever the Paystack dashboard has
# configured. Set it if you add a redirect checkout.
# NOTE: point this at a route that ACTUALLY EXISTS in your storefront. There is
# no /checkout/callback page in storefront/src/app today — you would have to add
# one. Leave commented until then rather than shipping a 404.
# FRONTEND_CALLBACK_URL=http://localhost:3009/<your-real-callback-route>

# How long an unpaid order holds its stock, in MILLISECONDS. Also drives the
# deadline quoted in the payment-failed email and the pending-payments sweep.
# OPTIONAL — falls back to 1800000 (30 minutes).
CART_RESTORATION_TIMEFRAME=1800000

# How long (ms) to keep waiting on a payment Paystack still reports as in progress (e.g. a bank
# transfer not yet confirmed) before the unpaid order is cancelled and its stock released. A payment
# that succeeds after that is refunded automatically and flagged for staff. OPTIONAL — default is
# 4× CART_RESTORATION_TIMEFRAME (2 hours).
# PAYMENT_MAX_WAIT_MS=7200000

# How long (ms) after delivery to email the review request. OPTIONAL — default 3 days.
# (Moved here from event-bus, where it was an in-memory timer.)
# RATING_REQUEST_DELAY=259200000


# ---- Storage / CDN (Bunny.net) ----

# Bunny storage zone name (the zone, not a URL).
# REQUIRED for any image/video upload — falls back to '' and every upload fails.
# Get it from: Bunny dashboard → Storage → your zone.
BUNNY_STORAGE_ZONE=<bunny-storage-zone-name>

# Bunny storage-zone password / access key (UUID-shaped).
# REQUIRED for uploads — falls back to '' (unauthenticated, all writes rejected).
# Get it from: Bunny dashboard → Storage → zone → FTP & API Access → Password.
BUNNY_ACCESS_KEY=xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx

# Bunny storage region, as an SDK region NAME (e.g. Falkenstein, NewYork,
# Singapore) — not a region code.
# OPTIONAL — empty or unrecognised values fall back to Falkenstein.
BUNNY_REGION=Falkenstein

# Public pull-zone base URL prefixed onto every uploaded asset path to build the
# `url`/`miniUrl`/`pngUrl` returned by FileUploadService.
# OPTIONAL — when unset those URL fields are simply omitted (only `path` is returned).
# NOTE: MUST include the scheme. The live .env has a schemeless host, which
# yields URLs like `<your-zone>.b-cdn.net/img.webp` that no browser will load —
# that is what scripts/fix-malformed-urls.ts exists to clean up.
BUNNY_BASE_URL=https://<your-zone>.b-cdn.net

# Public CDN base for images embedded in EMAIL and in the Google product feed
# (shared/emails/src/cdn-url.ts, FeedService, MerchantApiService).
# OPTIONAL — falls back to a legacy hardcoded b-cdn.net host baked into the code.
# Keep the trailing slash; the code appends one if missing.
CDN_BASE_URL=https://<your-zone>.b-cdn.net/


# ---- Email — SMTP transport ----
# Read by @rawura/emails (shared/emails/src/mailer.ts). Must be set on THIS service.

# SMTP server hostname.
# REQUIRED — no fallback; nodemailer cannot connect and no email is ever sent.
# Get it from: your ESP (MailerSend, Postmark, SES SMTP, …).
SMTP_HOST=smtp.<your-esp>.net

# SMTP port.
# OPTIONAL — falls back to 587. Use a STARTTLS port (587, or your ESP's alternate) here; 465 is implicit TLS.
SMTP_PORT=587

# SMTP username (often the full sending address).
# OPTIONAL in code (auth is omitted when both user and pass are unset), but
# REQUIRED by every real ESP.
SMTP_USER=<smtp-username>

# SMTP password / API token.
# OPTIONAL in code, REQUIRED in practice — see SMTP_USER.
SMTP_PASS=<smtp-password>

# Implicit TLS. Compared literally against the string 'true'.
# OPTIONAL — anything other than 'true' means false (STARTTLS). Set true only for port 465.
# REQUIRED — currently MISSING from .env; harmless today because the configured port wants
# STARTTLS, but it becomes wrong the moment the port changes to 465.
SMTP_SECURE=false

# Envelope From address for all outgoing mail. Also the fallback for the support
# address shown in email footers.
# OPTIONAL — falls back to the resolved brand support email.
# Must be a domain verified with your ESP or mail will be rejected.
FROM_EMAIL=<verified-sender@your-domain.com>

# Recompile Handlebars templates on every render instead of caching them.
# OPTIONAL — compared literally against '1'; anything else means cache on.
# Local template development only; never set in production.
EMAIL_TEMPLATE_NO_CACHE=0


# ---- Email — brand (resolved by src/services/brand/resolveBrand.ts) ----
# Resolution order for each of these is: Settings document → env var → hardcoded
# fallback. They only matter when the Settings document is missing or blank —
# which is exactly the case on a fresh clone, so set them.

# Store name in email headers, subjects and the pickup-contact block.
# OPTIONAL — falls back to 'Rawura'.
STORE_NAME=Rawura

# Legal company name in the email footer / copyright line.
# OPTIONAL — falls back to STORE_NAME.
# REQUIRED — currently MISSING from .env; footers show the store name instead of
# the registered entity.
COMPANY_NAME=<Registered Company Name Ltd>

# Absolute URL of the logo image at the top of every email.
# OPTIONAL — falls back to '' and the header renders with NO logo.
# REQUIRED — currently MISSING from .env; every email sent without a Settings
# document has a blank header.
STORE_LOGO_URL=https://<your-zone>.b-cdn.net/brand/logo.png

# Public storefront base URL. Every link in every email is built from it
# (order, tracking, product, cart, account, returns). Trailing slash is stripped.
# OPTIONAL — checked BEFORE FRONTEND_URL, then falls back to 'https://www.rawura.com'.
# REQUIRED — currently MISSING from .env; FeedService, MerchantApiService and all
# email links currently resolve via FRONTEND_URL instead, which points at
# localhost — meaning production emails could ship localhost links.
STOREFRONT_URL=http://localhost:3009

# Secondary storefront URL, used when STOREFRONT_URL is unset. Historically the
# only one set.
# OPTIONAL — same fallback chain as above.
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3009

# Public base URL of THIS API, used to build the one-click unsubscribe link.
# OPTIONAL — PUBLIC_API_URL is checked first, then API_URL, then ''.
# REQUIRED — currently MISSING from .env; brand.apiUrl resolves to '' so
# unsubscribeUrl() returns '' and marketing emails ship with NO unsubscribe link
# at all. That is a CAN-SPAM / GDPR exposure, not a cosmetic gap.
PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Alias for PUBLIC_API_URL, checked second.
# OPTIONAL — leave unset if PUBLIC_API_URL is set.
# API_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Customer-facing support email in the footer and "contact us" blocks.
# OPTIONAL — falls back to FROM_EMAIL, then 'support@rawura.com'.
# REQUIRED — currently MISSING from .env; footers currently print the raw ESP
# sending address, which is not a monitored inbox.
SUPPORT_EMAIL=support@<your-domain.com>

# Customer-facing support phone in emails.
# OPTIONAL — falls back to STORE_PHONE, then ''.
SUPPORT_PHONE=+234XXXXXXXXXX

# Store phone. Fallback for SUPPORT_PHONE, and the pickup contact number on
# pickup orders (src/services/email/orderEmailPayload.ts).
# OPTIONAL — falls back to '' (pickup emails show no contact number).
STORE_PHONE=+234XXXXXXXXXX

# Street address line 1. Used for the postal address in the email footer and as
# the pickup address on pickup orders when GIG sender config is absent.
# OPTIONAL — falls back to '' in email; to 'Store Pickup' on pickup orders.
STORE_ADDRESS=<street address>

# City for the footer postal address.
# OPTIONAL — falls back to ''.
STORE_CITY=<city>

# State/region for the footer postal address.
# OPTIONAL — falls back to ''.
STORE_STATE=<state>

# Country for the footer postal address.
# OPTIONAL — falls back to 'Nigeria'.
STORE_COUNTRY=Nigeria


# ---- Returns ----

# Address customers post approved returns to; printed in the return-approved email.
# OPTIONAL — falls back to the resolved brand address line, then omitted entirely.
# REQUIRED — currently MISSING from .env; combined with the unset STORE_ADDRESS
# above, approved-return emails tell the customer to ship the item nowhere.
RETURNS_ADDRESS=<returns dept, street, city, state>

# Packing instructions in the return-approved email.
# OPTIONAL — falls back to a sensible built-in sentence about original packaging
# and keeping proof of postage.
# RETURNS_INSTRUCTIONS=<custom packing instructions>


# ---- Orders ----

# Prefix on every generated human-readable order number (upper-cased by code).
# OPTIONAL — falls back to 'RW'. Changing it mid-flight produces two number
# formats in the same database; set it once, before the first order.
ORDER_NUMBER_PREFIX=RW


# ---- Messaging (RabbitMQ) ----

# AMQP connection URL for the event bus that event-bus and websocket-gateway
# consume (src/events/eventPublisher.ts).
# OPTIONAL — falls back to 'amqp://localhost:5672'. Use amqps:// for CloudAMQP.
# Get a hosted URL from: CloudAMQP dashboard → instance → AMQP URL.
RABBITMQ_URL=amqp://localhost:5672


# ---- Shipping (GIG Logistics) ----

# Base URL of the GIG third-party API.
# OPTIONAL — falls back to the GIG *dev/sandbox* host
# (https://dev-thirdpartynode.theagilitysystems.com). Production MUST override
# this or real shipments are booked against the sandbox.
GIG_API_URL=https://dev-thirdpartynode.theagilitysystems.com

# Access token for the GIG API. NOT an Authorization/Bearer header — GIGService.ts
# sends the raw value in an `access-token` request header, so paste the token
# exactly as GIG issues it, with no "Bearer " prefix.
# OPTIONAL — falls back to '' and every GIG call is rejected as unauthenticated.
# REQUIRED in practice — currently MISSING from .env; rate quotes, station lookup
# and shipment booking all fail. Get it from your GIG Logistics account manager.
GIG_ACCESS_TOKEN=<gig-api-bearer-token>


# ---- Integrations (Google Merchant Center) ----
# All optional as a block: MerchantApiService.isConfigured() gates every call, so
# the app runs fine with none of these set — product sync is simply off. It is
# entirely unconfigured in the live .env today.

# Google Merchant Center account id.
# OPTIONAL — falls back to ''; sync stays disabled.
# Get it from: Merchant Center → top-right account menu.
# GOOGLE_MERCHANT_ACCOUNT_ID=<numeric merchant id>

# API-managed product data source resource id.
# OPTIONAL — falls back to ''; sync stays disabled.
# Get it from: Merchant Center → Data sources.
# GOOGLE_MERCHANT_DATA_SOURCE=accounts/<account-id>/dataSources/<datasource-id>

# Feed label (country/market grouping) applied to synced products.
# OPTIONAL — falls back to 'NG'.
# GOOGLE_MERCHANT_FEED_LABEL=NG

# Path to a Google service-account JSON key file on disk. Standard GoogleAuth var.
# OPTIONAL — either this OR GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON must be present for
# isConfigured() to return true.
# Get it from: Google Cloud console → IAM → Service Accounts → Keys.
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/absolute/path/to/service-account.json

# The same service-account key inline, as a single-line JSON string. Preferred on
# hosts with no writable filesystem. JSON.parse'd at startup — malformed JSON throws.
# OPTIONAL — alternative to GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS.
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON={"type":"service_account","project_id":"...","private_key":"-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n","client_email":"...@....iam.gserviceaccount.com"}

# Cron expression for the scheduled product sync (src/cron/merchantSync.ts).
# OPTIONAL — falls back to '0 */6 * * *' (every 6 hours). Only runs when the
# Merchant credentials above are configured.
GOOGLE_MERCHANT_SYNC_CRON=0 */6 * * *

# Shared key protecting the manual /merchant/* sync routes; callers send it as
# the `x-merchant-key` header.
# OPTIONAL — when unset those routes return 503 'MERCHANT_SYNC_KEY not set',
# which is a safe closed default. Set it only if you want manual sync triggers.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# MERCHANT_SYNC_KEY=<32-char-hex>


# ---- Cross-service (on-demand cache revalidation) ----
# Fired from SettingsService.updateSettings so the Next.js apps drop their cached
# branding. Failures are swallowed — a wrong value degrades to a stale cache, not
# an error.

# Shared secret sent with the revalidation request. Must match the same variable
# in the storefront and admin apps.
# OPTIONAL — when unset, revalidation is skipped entirely.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
REVALIDATE_SECRET=<64-char-hex — must match storefront & admin>

# Storefront revalidation endpoint.
# OPTIONAL — skipped when unset.
STOREFRONT_REVALIDATE_URL=http://localhost:3009/api/revalidate-branding

# Admin revalidation endpoint.
# OPTIONAL — skipped when unset.
ADMIN_REVALIDATE_URL=http://localhost:4999/api/revalidate-branding

# Storefront cache-tag purge endpoint — the general one, used by every write path
# (products, sales, campaigns, categories, banners, intents, reviews, delivery
# settings), not just branding. See src/services/storefront/revalidate.ts.
# Point it at the CANONICAL host: the apex and the *.vercel.app alias both
# redirect, and a redirected POST loses its body.
# OPTIONAL — when unset, the storefront just falls back to its 12-hour schedule.
STOREFRONT_REVALIDATE_TAGS_URL=http://localhost:3009/api/revalidate


# ---- Unused ----
# Present in the live .env but read by NO code in src/ or scripts/. Listed here
# so nobody re-adds them thinking they matter. Delete from .env once confirmed
# no deploy platform or sibling service depends on them.
#
#   NIXPACKS_NODE_VERSION   Nixpacks/Railway BUILD-time pin, not app config.
#                           Keep it in the deploy platform, not in .env.
#   AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID       Dead S3 credentials — storage moved to Bunny.net.
#   AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY   Dead. A live secret sitting in .env for nothing.
#   AWS_REGION              Dead.
#   AWS_S3_BUCKET           Dead.
#   BCRYPT_SALT_ROUNDS      Ignored — src/lib/password.ts hardcodes SALT_ROUNDS = 10.
#   JWT_EXPIRES_IN          Ignored — expiry is passed per-call in tokenizer.ts.
#   JWT_REFRESH_EXPIRES_IN  Ignored — no refresh-token flow exists.
#   JWT_REFRESH_SECRET      Ignored — no refresh-token flow exists.
#   SESSION_SECRET          Ignored — this API is stateless/JWT; no session store.
#   RATE_LIMIT_MAX_REQUESTS Ignored — rate limiting is not wired to env.
#   RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS    Ignored.
#   PAYSTACK_PUBLIC_KEY     Belongs in the STOREFRONT, not here; the server only
#                           ever uses the secret key.
#   EVENT_BUS_URL           This service publishes to RabbitMQ; it never calls
#                           event-bus over HTTP.
#   WEBSOCKET_GATEWAY_URL   Same — the gateway consumes from RabbitMQ.
